L'employeur met en oeuvre les mesures pr:
The employer shall implement the measures provided for in Article L. 4121-1 on the basis of the following general principles of prevention:
1° Avoiding risks;
2° Assessing risks that cannot be avoided;
3° Combating risks at source;
4° Adapting work to the individual, in particular as regards the design of workstations and the choice of work equipment and of working and production methods, with a view in particular to limiting monotonous work and work at a predetermined pace and to reducing their effects on health;
5° Taking account of technical progress;
6° Replacing what is dangerous with what is not dangerous or less dangerous;
7° Planning prevention by integrating, into a coherent whole, technology, work organisation, working conditions, social relations and the influence of environmental factors, in particular the risks related to moral harassment and sexual harassment, as defined in Articles L. 1152-1 and L. 1153-1, as well as those related to sexist conduct defined in Article L. 1142-2-1;
8° Taking collective protection measures and giving them priority over individual protection measures;
9° Giving appropriate instructions to workers.

REGLEMENT INTERIEUR / fortement recomman:
INTERNAL RULES (RÈGLEMENT INTÉRIEUR) / strongly recommended
(Mandatory from 50 employees over 12 months)
The internal rules are a written document in which the employer sets out exclusively:
1° The measures for applying health and safety regulations in the company or establishment, in particular the instructions provided for in Article L. 4122-1;
2° The conditions under which employees may be called upon, at the employer's request, to take part in restoring working conditions that protect employees' health and safety, should these appear to be compromised;
3° The general and permanent rules on discipline, in particular the nature and scale of the sanctions the employer may impose.

L'employeur prend les mesures nécessaire:
The employer shall take the measures necessary so that any outbreak of fire can be fought quickly and effectively in the interest of rescuing workers.
These measures include in particular:
– firefighting equipment appropriate to the risks;
– an alarm system;
– safety instructions;
– periodic evacuation drills.

L'employeur veille à ce que les travaill:
The employer shall ensure that workers and the social and economic committee (CSE):
1° Receive information, in appropriate forms and periodically updated, on the hazardous chemical agents present in the workplace, such as, in particular, their names, the health and safety risks they pose and, where applicable, the occupational exposure limit values and biological limit values applicable to them;
2° Have access to the safety data sheets provided by the supplier of the chemical agents;
3° Receive training and information on the precautions to be taken to ensure their own protection and that of other workers present in the workplace. In particular, they are informed of the instructions relating to the hygiene measures to be observed and the use of personal protective equipment.
